---
import PNotes from "../components/PNotes.astro";
---

<p-slide class="cover-internal center">
  <h2 class="main-gradient">Let's see it assembled</h2>
  <p
    p-effect="from below"
    style="font-size: 0.7em; opacity: 0.8; margin-block-start: 0.8em;"
  >
    All layers. Running in the browser. Right now.
  </p>

  <PNotes>
    <p>
      This is the killer moment. Switch focus to the browser window with /demo
      open (or use the next slide's iframe).
    </p>
    <p>
      The talk title pays off here: "Less Build, More Runtime - The Modern CSS
      Approach to Design Systems".
    </p>
    <p>Everything we've seen so far leads to this.</p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>

<p-slide class="demo-live-slide">
  <iframe
    src="/demo"
    style="width: 100%; height: 88%; border: none; border-radius: 0.4rem;"
    title="Runtime CSS Design System - live demo"
  ></iframe>

  <PNotes>
    <p>SCRIPT - run IN ORDER:</p>
    <p>1. "Look at the left column - narrow container. Cards are stacked."</p>
    <p>
      2. "On the right the container is wide. :has(img) + @container trigger the
      two-column layout - zero modifier classes."
    </p>
    <p>
      3. "Hover a card. See the tint? That's color-mix() in oklch - the browser
      computes the tint from --accent live."
    </p>
    <p>
      4. "KILLER MOVE: change the Accent with the color picker. Border, hover
      tint - everything follows. ONE token. No rebuild."
    </p>
    <p>
      5. "Toggle dark/light. No duplicated media query - light-dark() does it in
      one line."
    </p>
    <p>6. "This is the flexible design system the title promised."</p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>

<p-slide class="demo-what-ran" autoplay timing-fragments="900">
  <h3 class="main-gradient center" style="margin-block-end: 1rem;">
    What just ran in the browser
  </h3>

  <dl>
    <div p-fragment p-effect="from left" timing-start="200">
      <dt>
        <code>@layer</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>cascade governata</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="from right" timing-start="200">
      <dt>
        <code>@property --accent</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>token tipizzato</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="from left" timing-start="500">
      <dt>
        <code>color-mix()</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>palette derivata live</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="from right" timing-start="500">
      <dt>
        <code>light-dark()</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>dark mode, una riga</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="from left" timing-start="800">
      <dt>
        <code>clamp()</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>spacing fluido</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="from right" timing-start="800">
      <dt>
        <code>@container</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>layout context-aware</dd>
    </div>

    <div p-fragment p-effect="zoom" timing-start="1100">
      <dt>
        <code>:has(img)</code>
      </dt>
      <dd>struttura come stato</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <PNotes>
    <p>Seven features. No build step for the dynamic part.</p>
    <p>
      Let them reveal one by one - the audience recognises them, they've seen
      them in action.
    </p>
    <p>Last note: this is not a prototype. This is how browsers work today.</p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>

<style lang="scss">
  .demo-live-slide {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 0.5rem !important;
  }

  .demo-what-ran {
    dl {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0.55em 1.5em;
      margin-block-start: 0.5em;
    }

    dl > div {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.12em;
    }

    dt {
      font-size: 0.65em;
      code {
        font-family: var(--talk-marco-graphik-medium, monospace);
        color: var(--main-sub-gradient-fallback, currentColor);
      }
    }

    dd {
      font-size: 0.48em;
      opacity: 0.8;
      margin: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
